        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <div><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #333333; font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;">Per CCR 249.3, this recruitment may be used to fill additional identical vacancies which occur within 180 days of the closing date of this bulletin.</span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"><br />Please note this is an &#39;Until Filled&#39; position. The application cut-off dates are March 31,2025, and April 11, 2025,&nbsp;11:59 PM (PST). Interested individuals must submit their application packages by the cut-off date to be considered.</span></p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">This position is headquartered in Sacramento, CA. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The Nutrition Services Division’s mission is to assist agencies with meeting the nutritional needs of school children in preschool through grade twelve and infants and children in childcare environments. Under the supervision of the Materials and Stores Supervisor at the State Distribution Center in Sacramento, the Heavy Truck Driver (HTD) is responsible for the operation of a two or three-axle truck tractor and pulling a 28- to 48-foot dry or refrigerated trailer. The HTD delivers U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) Foods and Department of Defense Fresh Fruit and Vegetables (DoD Fresh) to recipient agencies located in counties throughout Northern and Central California. The HTD loads the USDA Foods and DoD Fresh ensuring that the load is balanced in the trailer, and verifies the products and destination against the bill of lading prior to departure. The HTD is also responsible for contacting each location at minimum 48 hours prior to expected delivery, performing minor vehicle repairs and regular service maintenance to ensure the equipment is road worthy, keeping truck records, and preparing reports. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Occasional overnight travel and regular overtime are required. The HTD must meet Department of Motor Vehicle&#39;s requirements and is responsible for maintaining a class “A” commercial driver&#39;s license. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Free Parking</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Position is designated as safety sensitive and is subject to reasonable suspicion drug and alcohol testing.</span></div><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26308668&name=ProposedDutyStatement.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">IN OFFICE POSITION </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="color: #333333; font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">This position is headquartered in Sacramento and requires the incumbent to report to the office five days a week. This position is not eligible for telework.</span></p>
                </p>
            
</div>
        </div>

        <div class="jcBand">

            
                <div class="col col-half">
                    <h3 class="postingHeader">Minimum Requirements</h3>

                    <span id="lblMinimumReqsInClassSpec">You will find the Minimum Requirements in the Class Specification.</span><ul><li><a href='https://hrnet.calhr.ca.gov/CalHRNet/SpecCrossReference.aspx?ClassID=6378' target='_blank'>HEAVY TRUCK DRIVER</a></li></ul>
                </div>
            

            <div class="col col-half" style="vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Additional Documents</h3>

                <ul><li><a href='http://calcareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/Jobs/JobApplicationPackageChecklist.aspx?JobControlId=464492'>Job Application Package Checklist</a></li><li><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26308668&name=ProposedDutyStatement.pdf'>Duty Statement</a></li></ul>

